  "submitted_text": "Step 1: To find the sum of the coefficients of \\( g(x) \\), we can evaluate \\( g(1) \\). This is because substituting \\( x = 1 \\) into the polynomial gives the sum of its coefficients.\n\nStep 2: Since \\( g(x) = f(x-1) \\), we need to substitute \\( x = 1 \\) into \\( f(x-1) \\).\n\nStep 3: Substitute \\( x = 1 \\) into \\( f(x) = 3x^4 + 5x^2 - 9x - 2 \\):\n\\[ f(1-1) = f(0) = 3(0)^4 + 5(0)^2 - 9(0) - 2 = -2. \\]\n\nStep 4: Therefore, \\( g(1) = f(0) = -2 \\).\n\nFinal answer: \\boxed{-2}",
